Z||000006||theogre||03-07-2000||12:40 AM||||I ment what was making noise.............................. The blower is a cheap fix. The compressor ACC/Dryer and orifice isn't cheap but not hard. It's pretty well established that R134a runs just fine in Fiero. So recharging isn't a big deal either. That's if the compressor is really bad. If just the clutch is bad then it can be repiared without evacuating the system.<P>Just as likely the belt is crapped. that's about a 10$us fix.||||reg||1
Z||000007||GT Bastard||03-07-2000||01:51 AM||||It actually makes a fast grinding noise from the engine bay when I turn on the AC.  I'm guessing the bearings in the compressor?  ||||reg||1
Z||000008||Phaeton||03-07-2000||02:49 AM||||Sticking my ear really CLOSE to the screen.....sounds like it could be the pulley clutch or the compressor bearing, kinda hard to tell just listening through the screen.<BR>A trained ear would know.||||reg||1
Z||000009||theogre||03-07-2000||05:35 PM||||check the compressor pulley and clutch face and make sure it's not hitting on something. Take the belt off and make sure there is no wobble in the pulley. GM AC clutches aren't that well made. The magnet under the pulley could also be lose which would grind. A shot clutch disk can grind too. sometimes they get cruddy and slip or the magnet is weak and they slip.<P>Once you are certain it's not the clutch then worry about scrapping things. The clutch can be replaced seperatly and without evacing the system. You need a couple specialty tools but those aren't too hard to find. With the wheel and mud flap off it will be easier. Or you can carefully drop down the compresor where you can reach it.<P>The whole clutch is a single unit. Changing it is similar to changing the pulley on an alternator. The tools for this are usually in stock a pep boys and others. Some places even have loaner tools.<P>The clutch is available either/both carparts.com and wrenchead.com<P>You can check the compressor better by trying to turn it with a wrench. Turn it the same way it normally turns only. IF it is the compressor is making this much noise you'll likely feel it in the wrench handle as you turn.||||reg||1
